.claude/project_config/
.claude/rule_file/
.claude/spec_file/
.claude/template/
.agents/
# SkillMeat machine-local state (absolute paths; ledger stays on disk, untracked)
.claude/.skillmeat*
.skillmeat/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unbounded derived data — deliberately NOT committed (node_01M03EVAX5A6G0RZCT4NXSKTRQ)
#
# The six-hourly collector produced a single 80.2MB blob
# (raw/openai-codex/github-releases-*.json) against GitHub's 100MB hard limit,
# plus ~183MB of regenerable bundles. Both classes grow every run, and every
# byte committed to `main` is permanent. Two rules decide what stays:
#
#   1. Content-addressed upstream API caches are an audit trail nothing reads.
#      `raw_snapshot_path` is None for every github/npm/pypi collector record
#      (hcr/collectors/{github_releases,package_registries}.py), so untracking
#      them loses no provenance the registry itself does not already carry via
#      `raw_sha256` + `source_url`. They remain on disk after a collect.
#   2. Bundles are deterministic outputs of `build_bundle()` — byte-identical on
#      regeneration from unchanged input (hcr/generators/bundle.py). Rebuild with
#      `make generate`; the test suite calls build_bundle() itself, so a clean
#      clone still validates.
#
# NOT ignored, and do not add them: raw/*/CHANGELOG.md (referenced by
# `raw_snapshot_path` for 208 releases) and raw/source-snapshots/ (the doc-drift
# dedup in _snapshot_source() compares against the newest committed *.meta.json —
# untracking it would make every source report `changed` on every CI run).
raw/*/github-releases-*.json
raw/*/npm-*.json
raw/*/pypi-*.json
app/data/registry.bundle.json
app/data/registry.bundle.js
generated/registry.bundle.json
generated/Harness_Matrix_Standalone.html
